@TITLE Lone Wolf: Flight from the Dark
@AUTHOR Adapted from Joe Dever (Project Aon)
@START burning_monastery
@DESC_TEXT Flee the destroyed Kai monastery to reach Holmgard.

@ROOM burning_monastery
@DESC
The Kai monastery burns. Screams
echo through smoke-filled halls as
Darklord armies swarm the grounds.
You are the last Kai Lord alive.
You must escape now or perish.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Search the armory" -> armory
@CHOICE "Climb the outer wall" -> monastery_wall
@CHOICE "Run through the fire" -> fire_run

@ROOM fire_run
@DESC
You dash through a curtain of flame.
Burning timbers crash around you.
A beam strikes your shoulder and
you stumble but keep running. You
burst through a shattered window.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET wounded
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Flee to the forest" -> forest_edge

@ROOM armory
@DESC
The armory is ablaze. Racks of
weapons have toppled. Through the
smoke you spot a Kai sword still
on its mount. The ceiling groans
above you.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM sword "Kai Sword" "A finely balanced blade bearing the Kai crest."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Grab sword and flee" -> monastery_wall @SET has_sword
@CHOICE "Search for more" -> armory_collapse

@ROOM armory_collapse
@DESC
You linger too long. The burning
rafters give way with a thunderous
crack. Tons of flaming debris
crash down upon you.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Greed cost you your life. Take what you can and flee!"

@ROOM monastery_wall
@DESC
You scale the outer wall and drop
into soft grass beyond. Behind you
the monastery is a roaring inferno.
Giak war-horns sound in the valley.
The forest ahead offers cover.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Enter the forest" -> forest_edge

@ROOM forest_edge
@DESC
Ancient pines tower above you. The
sounds of battle fade behind. Two
trails lead deeper into Dorier
forest. The north trail is wider.
The south trail is overgrown.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Take the north trail" -> forest_path_north
@CHOICE "Take the south trail" -> forest_clearing

@ROOM forest_path_north
@DESC
You follow the northern trail. Boot
prints in the mud -- Giak patrol.
The tracks are fresh. Guttural
voices drift from around the bend.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Hide in the bushes" -> hidden_safe
@CHOICE "Keep walking" -> giak_ambush
@CHOICE "Throw rocks at them" -> giak_rocks

@ROOM hidden_safe
@DESC
You crouch behind dense bracken
as three Giaks march past. Their
yellow eyes scan the trail but
miss you entirely. When they pass
you slip away southward.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET avoided_giaks
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Continue south" -> forest_clearing

@ROOM giak_ambush
@DESC
Three Giaks leap from the trees!
Their crude swords slash the air.
They snarl and circle you with
murderous intent.
@IF has_sword
Your Kai sword gleams as you draw
it into a fighting stance.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Fight with sword" -> giak_fight @NEED sword
@CHOICE "Run for your life" -> giak_flee

@ROOM giak_fight
@DESC
Your Kai training takes over. You
parry the first strike and cut
down the lead Giak. The other two
hesitate, then flee howling into
the trees. The path is clear.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET giaks_defeated
@SCORE +25
@CHOICE "Continue south" -> forest_clearing

@ROOM giak_flee
@DESC
You turn and sprint through the
undergrowth. Branches lash your
face. A Giak blade catches your
leg and you stumble but break free.
Blood soaks your trouser leg.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET wounded
@CHOICE "Limp onward" -> forest_clearing

@ROOM giak_rocks
@DESC
You hurl stones from the roadside
at the Giaks. One takes a rock to
the skull and drops. The others
scatter in confusion, thinking
an ambush. You slip past them.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +15
@CHOICE "Continue south" -> forest_clearing

@ROOM forest_clearing
@DESC
A clearing in the pines. A dead
merchant lies beside an overturned
cart. His wares are scattered in
the grass. Poor soul -- Giaks
got him.
@ENDDESC
@ITEM gold_coins "Gold Coins" "A leather purse heavy with gold crowns."
@ITEM healing_potion "Healing Potion" "A green glass vial labeled Laumspur."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Continue down the road" -> forest_stream

@ROOM forest_stream
@DESC
A swift stream crosses the trail.
Stepping stones lead across the
shallow water. Downstream you
can see an old stone bridge half
hidden by ivy.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Wade across the stream" -> hermit_cabin
@CHOICE "Go to the bridge" -> old_bridge

@ROOM old_bridge
@DESC
A rickety stone bridge spans the
stream. Several stones are missing
and the mortar crumbles at your
touch. It looks treacherous.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Cross carefully" -> hermit_cabin
@CHOICE "Run across quickly" -> bridge_collapse

@ROOM bridge_collapse
@DESC
Your weight is too much. The
ancient stones give way beneath
you and you plunge into the rocky
gorge below. The fall is fatal.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Haste and old bridges do not mix. Cross with care!"

@ROOM hermit_cabin
@DESC
A woodsman's cabin sits in a quiet
glade. Smoke curls from the chimney.
Herb gardens line the path to a
sturdy oak door. It looks peaceful.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Knock on the door" -> hermit_inside
@CHOICE "Pass by quietly" -> graveyard_hill

@ROOM hermit_inside
@DESC
A kind old hermit welcomes you. He
sees your Kai cloak and bows. He
offers you a hot meal and a rough
map of the road to Holmgard.
"Stay off the hilltops," he warns.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET hermit_friend
@ON_ENTER @GIVE meal "Meal" "Bread, cheese, and dried meat wrapped in cloth."
@ON_ENTER @GIVE map "Map" "A rough map marking the road to Holmgard."
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Thank him and leave" -> graveyard_hill @SET has_map

@ROOM graveyard_hill
@DESC
The trail climbs over a barren
hill dotted with ancient graves.
Weathered stone markers lean at
odd angles. A shadow passes over
you -- Kraan circle overhead!
@ENDDESC
@ITEM shield "Shield" "A battered wooden shield from an old grave."
@CHOICE "Hide among the graves" -> graveyard_hide @SET has_shield
@CHOICE "Run downhill" -> kraan_attack

@ROOM graveyard_hide
@DESC
You press yourself behind a tall
gravestone. The Kraan shriek and
circle but cannot spot you among
the stones. After long minutes
they wheel away to the north.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Descend the far slope" -> heal_spring

@ROOM kraan_attack
@DESC
A Kraan dives at you with talons
spread! Its shadow blots out the
sun. You have a split second to
react.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Dive to the left" -> kraan_dodge
@CHOICE "Dive to the right" -> kraan_caught

@ROOM kraan_dodge
@DESC
You throw yourself left and roll
behind a boulder. The Kraan's
talons rake the dirt where you
stood. It shrieks and climbs
away, seeking easier prey.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Hurry downhill" -> heal_spring

@ROOM kraan_caught
@DESC
The Kraan snatches you up in its
iron talons. It carries you high
above the forest then releases
you over the treetops.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Kraan are deadly. Hide from what you cannot fight!"

@ROOM heal_spring
@DESC
At the base of the hill a clear
spring bubbles from mossy rocks.
The water sparkles with an almost
magical shimmer. The road to the
river lies ahead.
@IF wounded
Your wounds throb painfully. The
spring water might help, or you
could use your healing potion.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Drink from the spring" -> heal_spring_drink
@CHOICE "Continue to the river" -> river_bank @NEED !wounded
@CHOICE "Limp to the river" -> river_bank_wounded @NEED wounded

@ROOM heal_spring_drink
@DESC
The spring water is ice cold and
tastes faintly of herbs. Warmth
spreads through your body. Your
wounds begin to close. You feel
renewed strength in your limbs.
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET healed
@SCORE +5
@CHOICE "Continue to the river" -> river_bank

@ROOM river_bank
@DESC
The Dorier River stretches wide
before you. The current is strong
but the far bank is visible. A
ferry landing lies downstream with
a small boat tied to the dock.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Swim across" -> river_swim
@CHOICE "Go to the ferry" -> river_ferry

@ROOM river_bank_wounded
@DESC
The Dorier River stretches wide
before you. Your wounds ache and
the current looks deadly. No way
you can swim this. A ferry landing
lies downstream. That's your path.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Go to the ferry" -> river_ferry

@ROOM river_swim
@DESC
You plunge into the cold water
and swim hard against the current.
Your Kai training serves you well.
Gasping, you drag yourself onto
the far bank. Holmgard awaits.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Follow the road" -> road_to_holmgard

@ROOM river_ferry
@DESC
A weathered ferryman eyes you from
his small boat. "Two gold crowns
to cross," he growls, spitting
into the river. "No coin, no
ride. That's the way of it."
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Pay the ferryman" -> ferry_cross @NEED gold_coins @USE gold_coins
@CHOICE "Use healing potion" -> potion_heal @NEED healing_potion
@CHOICE "Threaten the ferryman" -> ferry_threat

@ROOM potion_heal
@DESC
You drink the Laumspur potion.
Warmth floods your body and your
wounds knit together. The pain
fades to nothing. You feel whole
again. Now about that river...
@ENDDESC
@ON_ENTER @SET healed
@CHOICE "Swim across" -> river_swim @USE healing_potion
@CHOICE "Threaten the ferryman" -> ferry_threat

@ROOM ferry_cross
@DESC
The ferryman pockets your gold and
poles you across the wide river.
"Giaks on the north road," he
mutters. "Best go south through
the farmlands." You thank him.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "Follow the road" -> road_to_holmgard

@ROOM ferry_threat
@DESC
You raise your fist at the old
ferryman. He blows a whistle and
three armed men emerge from the
reeds. They are not pleased.
You are overwhelmed.
@ENDDESC
@GAMEOVER "Violence against civilians wins no allies. Try gold instead!"

@ROOM road_to_holmgard
@DESC
The King's Highway stretches south
toward Holmgard. Refugees stream
along the road -- farmers, women,
children fleeing the Darklands
invasion. The city is close now.
@IF has_map
Your map shows a shortcut through
the western forest to the gates.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Join the refugees" -> refugee_column
@CHOICE "Take forest shortcut" -> forest_shortcut

@ROOM refugee_column
@DESC
You march with the refugees. An
old soldier recognizes your Kai
cloak and salutes. Children stare
with wide eyes. The column moves
slowly but safely toward the city.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +10
@CHOICE "March to the gates" -> holmgard_gates

@ROOM forest_shortcut
@DESC
You leave the road and enter the
western woods. The trees are thick
and the path fades quickly.
@IF has_map
The hermit's map shows the way
clearly. You navigate with ease.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the map" -> shortcut_success @NEED map
@CHOICE "Navigate by instinct" -> lost_forest

@ROOM shortcut_success
@DESC
The hermit's map guides you true.
You emerge from the forest within
sight of Holmgard's great stone
walls. The shortcut saved you
hours of travel.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +20
@CHOICE "Approach the gates" -> holmgard_gates

@ROOM lost_forest
@DESC
Without a map the forest is a
maze of identical pines. You
wander for hours before stumbling
onto the highway again. Precious
time wasted, but you are alive.
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Follow the road" -> holmgard_gates

@ROOM holmgard_gates
@DESC
The great stone gates of Holmgard
rise before you. Soldiers line the
battlements. A captain descends
the steps and approaches you.
"Halt! State your business!"
@IF has_sword
He eyes your Kai sword with
recognition and respect.
@ENDIF
@ENDDESC
@CHOICE "Show your Kai cloak" -> victory
@CHOICE "Demand entry" -> victory

@ROOM victory
@DESC
The captain sees your Kai cloak
and gasps. "A Kai Lord lives!"
Word spreads like wildfire. You
are rushed to the throne room
where King Dorain himself greets
you. The last Kai Lord has reached
Holmgard. Sommerlund has hope.
@ENDDESC
@SCORE +30
@WIN "You reached Holmgard alive! The last Kai Lord endures. Score: {score}"
